From 91e48de2fb54e3cfb768b7fa747f43204b4d8265 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Colliers <mail@thomascolliers.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 15:41:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] media: qcom: camss: Add SM7635 resources and compatible

Add the CSIPHY, CSID and VFE resources for the Qualcomm milos (SM7635)
SoC, along with the qcom,milos-camss compatible.

Each CSIPHY votes a load on the two PHY supplies for as long as it is
streaming. The values come from the downstream volcano-camera.dtsi,
which reserves 98480 uA on the 0.9V rail and 17920 uA on the 1.2V rail
per PHY.

Only the RDI lines are wired up. The PIX path drives the pixel
processing crop block, which on TFE530 is the post-BDS crop at 0x2800
from the TFE base. TFE665 has a rather different pixel pipeline: the
equivalent block is a different module sitting at 0x5200, and even the
CAMIF moves from 0x200 to 0x400. Exposing a PIX video device before
that path has been worked out and tested on hardware would only offer
a node that cannot produce frames, so line_num stays at 3.

Tested on a Fairphone 6 (SM7635) with an OmniVision OV13B10 on CSIPHY1.

Assisted-by: pi:claude-opus-5
Suggested-by: Jorijn van der Graaf <jorijnvdgraaf@catcrafts.net>
Signed-off-by: Thomas Colliers <mail@thomascolliers.com>
